Topic 4.1: Sanan's Space-Time FDM Hypothesis and The Ghost Signal (สมมติฐาน Space-Time FDM และวงจรกรองจักรวาล)
[English]
Sanan's Space-Time Frequency-Division Multiplexing (FDM) Hypothesis redefines the universe. Instead of branching chronological timelines (Parallel Universes), the universe operates as an advanced RF broadcasting system. All physical matter at the present moment ($t_0$) is modulated onto a massive global baseline carrier wave ($F_0$). Time progression is driven by the continuous shifting of this fundamental carrier frequency.
The reason we only experience the present is due to the "Cosmic Bandpass Filter," a natural quantum filter that isolates the current time and rejects the carrier frequencies of the past ($-Z$) and future ($+Z$). The past and future exist concurrently on the exact same spatial coordinates but operate on entirely separate frequency channels.
If a physical mass (a traveler) shifts into past coordinates without a precise "Field Impedance Match," its atomic structure fails to lock onto the past carrier wave. The payload retains its original $F_0$ resonance. Consequently, the traveler acts as an out-of-phase noise wave—a Ghost Signal. In this state, they are completely invisible, unable to interact mechanically, pass through solid objects without collision, and are incapable of altering past historical data.
